    "comparison": "All three candidate claims are supported within their stated hypotheses and scopes: the first is an elliptic-curve obstruction for the specified canonical order-three seed, the second is an exact reduction for opposite-sign anchors and a symmetric paired configuration, and the third is a local denominator-residue restriction. None resolves the original sextuple existence problem. In particular, candidate one leaves appended-coordinate and other construction cases open; candidate two does not address the all-positive case or arbitrary nonsymmetric neighbors; candidate three does not establish a universal four-neighbor obstruction. The supplied finite searches remain bounded or mechanism-specific and cannot close those gaps."
